              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for the tow truck, then the German for the mechanic."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Reifen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Reifen — \"the tyre (US: tire)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im Herbst wechseln wir die Reifen. In autumn we change the tyres."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Same form in the plural. Die Winterreifen — winter tyres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Reifen goes back to Reif 'ring, hoop', inherited from Old High German reif 'band, ring' (EtymDB). EtymDB links it with English rope, from the same Germanic word for a band."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
